.TH CYAML_CREATE_NULL_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_create_null_mp, cyaml_create_null \- allocate a YAML null node
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

cyaml cyaml_create_null_mp(ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mp);
cyaml cyaml_create_null(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Allocate a DOM node of type CYAML_NULL.  cyaml_create_null() is an
inline wrapper.  It passes NULL to cyaml_create_null_mp(), and that
selects the default allocator.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
mp   Custom memory management procedures, or NULL for the default
     allocator.
     The library keeps its own copy of the struct, so the caller may
     release or reuse the struct once this call returns. The functions
     that it names must stay callable until the last node built with
     them is destroyed. A process can use at most 64 distinct sets of
     four functions; a call that would need a 65th fails and returns
     NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
New cyaml node on success, NULL on allocation failure.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_destroy (3),
.BR cyaml_type (3)
